<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap narrow-wrap prose-page">
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you request to attend or send an inquiry, we receive what you enter in the form: your name, title, position, organization, email address, phone number, country and city, the sessions you plan to attend, the names and details of any guests you add, any dietary or accessibility needs you tell us about, press outlet details if you are media, and your message.</p>
    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <p>We use these details to review requests to attend, confirm places, prepare access lists, plan seating and catering, meet accessibility needs, issue press credentials, and contact you about the Summit. If you ask for news of future Summits, we will also use your email address for that.</p>
    <h2>Who sees it</h2>
    <p>Your details are seen by the Summit organizers and the collaborating organizations named on this site. Names may be shared with venue and security staff where that is needed for entry. We do not sell your details or share them for marketing.</p>
    <h2>How the forms work</h2>
    <p>Form submissions are delivered to the organizers by email through Web3Forms, a form delivery service.</p>
    <h2>Photography, filming, and broadcast</h2>
    <p>The Summit will be photographed and filmed, and it may be broadcast or livestreamed. Recordings, photographs, and the texts of addresses may be published on this site.</p>
    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>We keep your details only as long as needed to organize the Summit and its follow-up. Dietary and accessibility details are deleted after the event.</p>
    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You may ask to see, correct, or delete the details we hold about you at any time through the <a href="{{ '/contact/' | url }}">contact form</a>.</p>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>This site does not use advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
    <p class="small">Last updated November 2026.</p>
  </div>
</section>
